  "caption": "Quinn's niece Juno, 15, blamed her phone for a sore neck, so Quinn tried her routine: hours of scrolling, homework on the bed and late-night videos. Quinn's neck asked for help.\n\nScreens aren't harming teen spines for good. Neck pain is linked to screen time, but long still positions, low activity, poor sleep, stress and low neck endurance often matter more.\n\nWhat can help: breaks about every 30 minutes, regular activity they enjoy, neck and upper-back endurance exercises, devices out of the bedroom, and a raised screen with a separate keyboard for study.\n\nGet it checked for night pain, arm pain, numbness or weakness, pain after an injury, severe or changing headaches, fever or weight loss, or pain that's limiting school.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
